\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The \textsc  {Aegis}\xspace  pipeline. Inputs (left) flow through four layers: (1)~Graph Processing (BFS subgraph extraction, forward pass or fixed-point convergence), (2)~Sensitivity Computation (dense Jacobian path for $N \leq 200$; matrix-free Neumann/JVP path for larger graphs), (3)~Constrained Projection ($N^2 \to |E|$ reduction via $P_c$), and (4)~Vulnerability Analysis (randomized SVD, column norms of $S_c$, per-node radii). The matrix-free formulation operates via JVP/VJP queries without materializing $S$ or $S_c$, enabling full-graph analysis (tested up to $N{=}7{,}650$).}}{7}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{1}{7}{The \AEGIS pipeline. Inputs (left) flow through four layers: (1)~Graph Processing (BFS subgraph extraction, forward pass or fixed-point convergence), (2)~Sensitivity Computation (dense Jacobian path for $N \leq 200$; matrix-free Neumann/JVP path for larger graphs), (3)~Constrained Projection ($N^2 \to |E|$ reduction via $P_c$), and (4)~Vulnerability Analysis (randomized SVD, column norms of $S_c$, per-node radii). The matrix-free formulation operates via JVP/VJP queries without materializing $S$ or $S_c$, enabling full-graph analysis (tested up to $N{=}7{,}650$)}{figure.caption.2}{}}
\newlabel{fig:pipeline@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][6][]7}{}{}{}}
